 "notes": "ROS 1 description-only package: no topics, services, actions or params in the packet. All ten packet elements are consumed resources, referenced as <mesh filename=...> in urdf/sia5d_macro.xacro (source) and identically in the generated urdf/sia5d.urdf (lines 12,18,26,32,48,69,90,111,132,153). Nothing is provided, so declares and not_declared are empty. The referenced files exist in the snapshot at motoman_config/meshes/sia5/{visual,collision}/ (motoman_config 0.3.3). frame = the URDF link the mesh is attached to, verbatim from the xacro macro (origin xyz=0 rpy=0); in the generated sia5d.urdf the prefix is empty (base_link, link_s, ...). units null: the xacro sets no <mesh scale> and the referenced .dae files contain no <unit> element (they declare <up_axis>Y_UP</up_axis> at line 8). QoS null (ROS 1). definition_id null: meshes are not msg/srv/action/idl definitions, so definition_hash.py does not apply. package.xml run_depends: motoman_driver, robot_state_publisher, rviz, joint_state_publisher; no motoman_config. The package's own meshes/sia5d/{visual,collision}/*.dae (installed by CMakeLists.txt:13-16) are byte-identical (sha1) to motoman_config/meshes/sia5/* but unreferenced. Other references not in the packet: $(find xacro)/xacro.py (launch/load_sia5d.launch:3), $(find motoman_driver)/launch/robot_interface_streaming_$(arg controller).launch and robot_state_$(arg controller).launch, $(find industrial_robot_client)/config/robot_state_visualize.rviz; it sets param robot_description and loads controller_joint_names from config/joint_names_sia5d.yaml. Minor: robot_state_visualize_sia5d.launch:9 usage comment says sia20d."
